    <ShortLegislativeSummaryEn>A legislative summary is currently being prepared for this bill by the Parliamentary Information and Research Service of the Library of Parliament. Meanwhile, the following executive summary is available. 

On 13 May 2010, The Minister of Foreign Affairs introduced Bill C-26, An Act to amend the International Boundary Waters Treaty Act and the International River Improvements Act (Transboundary Waters Protection Act), in the House of Commons and it was given first reading.

Bill C-26 amends the International Boundary Waters Treaty Act to prohibit the bulk removal of transboundary waters. Some definitions and exceptions that are currently found in regulations are transferred to Bill C-26. The Act gives the federal government powers of inspection and enforcement and introduces penalties for violations, including monetary fines. The enactment also provides for measures to administer and enforce the Act. Lastly, it also makes a consequential amendment to the International River Improvements Act.</ShortLegislativeSummaryEn>
    <ShortLegislativeSummaryFr>Le Service d'information et de recherche parlementaires de la Bibliothèque du Parlement rédige actuellement le résumé législatif de ce projet de loi et vous propose en attendant le sommaire suivant.

Le 13 mai 2010, le ministre des Affaires étrangères a présenté à la Chambre des communes le projet de loi C-26, Loi modifiant la Loi du traité des eaux limitrophes internationales et la Loi sur les ouvrages destinés à l'amélioration des cours d'eau internationaux (Loi sur la protection des eaux transfrontalières), qui a franchi l'étape de la première lecture.

Le projet de loi C-26 modifie la Loi du traité des eaux limitrophes internationales en vue d'interdire le captage massif d'eaux transfrontalières. Certaines définitions et exceptions se trouvant dans les règlements sont incluses dans la loi. Le projet de loi C-26 donne au gouvernement fédéral des pouvoirs en matière d'inspection et d'application de la loi, et en cas d'infraction, elle prévoit également des sanctions, y compris des amendes monétaires. De plus, le texte prévoit des mesures d'exécution et de contrôle d'application de la loi. Enfin, il modifie la Loi sur les ouvrages destinés à l'amélioration des cours d'eau internationaux en conséquence.</ShortLegislativeSummaryFr>
    <ShortLegislativeSummary>A legislative summary is currently being prepared for this bill by the Parliamentary Information and Research Service of the Library of Parliament. Meanwhile, the following executive summary is available. 

On 13 May 2010, The Minister of Foreign Affairs introduced Bill C-26, An Act to amend the International Boundary Waters Treaty Act and the International River Improvements Act (Transboundary Waters Protection Act), in the House of Commons and it was given first reading.

Bill C-26 amends the International Boundary Waters Treaty Act to prohibit the bulk removal of transboundary waters. Some definitions and exceptions that are currently found in regulations are transferred to Bill C-26. The Act gives the federal government powers of inspection and enforcement and introduces penalties for violations, including monetary fines. The enactment also provides for measures to administer and enforce the Act. Lastly, it also makes a consequential amendment to the International River Improvements Act.</ShortLegislativeSummary>
